#!/usr/bin/env bash
cat <<'EOF'
bin/xdebug has been removed.

Xdebug is still cookie-triggered (XDEBUG_SESSION) — that part hasn't
changed. What's changed is where the extension lives: it's no longer
loaded into the main phpfpm container. A dedicated phpfpm-xdebug
container runs alongside, and nginx routes requests to it only when
the XDEBUG_SESSION cookie is set.

The result: requests without the cookie never load xdebug at all, so
there's nothing to toggle on/off — keep the cookie set, browse at full
speed, debug whenever you flip the cookie on.

CLI:
  bin/debug-cli <command>    # runs in the phpfpm-xdebug container
  bin/cli <command>          # runs in the clean phpfpm container

See README -> Xdebug for IDE setup.
EOF
exit 1
